sequenceDiagram
    participant Clients
    participant API
    participant Cache
    participant Mutex as Distributed Lock
    participant DB

    Note over Clients,DB: Cache Breakdown (Thundering Herd) & Singleflight Mitigation
    
    Note over Cache: Key "viral_tweet_123" Expires
    
    par 1000 Concurrent Requests
        Clients->>API: GET /tweet/123
        API->>Cache: GET "viral_tweet_123"
        Cache-->>API: Miss
    end
    
    Note over API: All threads attempt to acquire lock
    
    API->>Mutex: Try Acquire Lock "lock:tweet_123"
    
    alt Thread 1 (Wins Lock)
        Mutex-->>API: Lock Acquired
        API->>DB: Query Tweet 123 (Only 1 query hits DB!)
        DB-->>API: Tweet Data
        API->>Cache: SET "viral_tweet_123" = Data
        API->>Mutex: Release Lock
        API-->>Clients: Return Data
    else Thread 2-1000 (Lose Lock)
        Mutex-->>API: Lock Failed
        Note over API: Threads wait/poll for cache population
        loop Retry Cache
            API->>Cache: GET "viral_tweet_123"
            alt After Thread 1 Completes
                Cache-->>API: Tweet Data (Hit)
            end
        end
        API-->>Clients: Return Data
    end
